      "id": "12j54st",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Discovery of the Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Robert Hooke discovered cells in 1665 while examining a thin slice of cork under a microscope.",
        "Schleiden and Schwann formulated the Cell Theory, which Rudolf Virchow expanded with the concept 'Omnis cellula-e-cellula'.",
        "Prokaryotic cells lack a membrane-bound nucleus, whereas Eukaryotic cells contain a distinct nucleus and membrane-bound organelles.",
        "Mitochondria generate cellular energy in the form of ATP and are known as the powerhouse of the cell.",
        "Plant cells possess a rigid cellulose cell wall, large central vacuole, and plastids, which are absent in animal cells."
      ],
      "id": "pctrwmq"
    },
