    {
      "id": "4vd85my",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Difference Between Plant Cell and Animal Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Ribosomes are non-membrane bound organelles found in both prokaryotic (70S) and eukaryotic (80S) cells.",
        "Mitochondria and Chloroplasts are semi-autonomous organelles containing their own circular DNA and 70S ribosomes.",
        "Lysosomes are commonly called 'Suicide Bags' due to the presence of acidic hydrolytic digestive enzymes.",
        "Plant cell walls are made of cellulose, whereas fungal cell walls consist of chitin."
      ],
      "id": "7xragie"
    },
